    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2019-boundary-14: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.85";
    dc:description "The claim maps to standard comparative sequence and channel-function analyses supported by large public databases. Its universal wording needs interpretation, but broad coverage and direct homolog tests make it resolvable now.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For ion channels mediating each named animal sense, identify bacterial homologues, reconstruct their evolutionary relationships, and compare conserved domains, gating mechanisms, and sensory functions; absence of homologous mechanisms for major modalities would refute the broad statement.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Exact same mechanism may mean homology, biophysical principle, or molecular identity.", "Functional annotation quality varies strongly in bacteria.";
